Write 2-4 procedures that let staff run the pilot with ONLY what exists today: phones, the messaging channels the client already uses, spreadsheets, and the client's current tools. Cover between them: selecting eligible orders and assigning treatment vs control; the manual outreach itself (message send, response handling, consent and opt-out); recording results in the pilot log; and the daily review with escalation and the gate-review closeout.

Rules per procedure:
- phase is ALWAYS "pilot".
- Every step is executable today — no dashboards, portals, AI agents, or unbuilt modules anywhere. The actor is "you" or a real staff role; never "ai". Never name any module listed above inside a step.
- ASSIGNMENT is the canonical design and nothing else: comparable eligible orders are randomized 50/50 between treatment and control (e.g. a random number per order in the log) — never by client, zone, day, previous period or alternation.
- A client-stated policy keeps its event origin exactly ("10 days after month-end" stays "after month-end").
- Success criteria restate the pilot gate verbatim — never invent alternate thresholds.
- THRESHOLDS: any time window, retry count or cut-off is either a client-stated fact or carries "(proposed — client approval required)". One canonical value per condition — the same wait may never appear as two different numbers.
- Consent: the first outreach message identifies the business and offers an opt-out; an opted-out customer is never contacted again during the pilot.
- Records: name the exact columns of the pilot log a spreadsheet needs.
